00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:26.040
Imagine you bought an Energy ETF last week when BLS data highlighted strong job growth in the sector.

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:38.280
Your order filled at the market price, but the actual mechanics between the click and the fill involve bid-ask spreads that can widen from 2 cents to 15 cents in the first 30 minutes of a news-driven session.

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:43.840
A call option gives the buyer the right to purchase the underlying at a set strike while

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:48.680
a put gives the right to sell, with the premium split between intrinsic value based on the

00:03:48.680 --> 00:03:52.400
current price versus strike and time value that decays daily.

00:03:53.380 --> 00:03:58.380
Professionals always check the Greeks, especially theta for time decay and delta for directional

00:03:58.380 --> 00:04:03.160
exposure before entering a covered call that collects premium on shares they already

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:08.140
own or a cash-secured put that commits capital only if the price drops to the strike.

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:13.580
Most retail investors do not realize that naked options can lead to unlimited losses

00:04:13.580 --> 00:04:18.240
while covered strategies cap both upside and downside in predictable ways.

00:04:18.980 --> 00:04:24.340
The concrete misconception to avoid is treating options as simple directional bets instead of

00:04:24.340 --> 00:04:25.860
income or protection tools.

00:04:26.560 --> 00:04:32.040
The fix is to start every options trade by calculating the exact capital at risk and the

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:34.740
The premium received at the quoted strike and expiry.

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:41.300
Covered calls work best on names already owned inside a TFSA where the investor is comfortable

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:42.860
with assignment near the strike.

00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:48.180
Cash secured puts require the investor to have the full capital ready at the strike price

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:49.680
in case assignment occurs.

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:55.920
Time decay accelerates in the final 30 days before expiry, so theta becomes the dominant

00:04:55.920 --> 00:04:56.800
Greek to monitor.

00:04:56.800 --> 00:05:02.920
The bid asks spread on options can be wider than on the underlying shares, so liquidity checks

00:05:02.920 --> 00:05:04.320
are essential before entry.

